# RLS Policy Recursion Fix for Code Arena

We detected an infinite recursion bug under PostgreSQL due to RLS policies on `coding_battles` and `coding_battle_participants` referencing each other circularly.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Layer (Supabase)

#### [NEW] [087_fix_code_arena_rls_recursion.sql](file:///d:/Institute/BCE/supabase/migrations/087_fix_code_arena_rls_recursion.sql)

Create a new migration establishing:
1. Four new `security definer` helper functions that bypass RLS checks internally when querying battle states:
   - `public.code_arena_is_battle_creator(battle_uuid, user_uuid)`
   - `public.code_arena_is_battle_participant(battle_uuid, student_uuid)`
   - `public.code_arena_is_battle_live_participant(battle_uuid, student_uuid)`
   - `public.code_arena_can_join_battle(battle_uuid, student_uuid)` (includes student-count `< 25` limit check)
2. Replacements for the 7 circular/problematic RLS policies across `coding_battles`, `coding_battle_problems`, `coding_battle_participants`, and `coding_submissions`.

---

### Migration Runner

#### [NEW] [apply_087.ts](file:///d:/Institute/BCE/src/scripts/apply_087.ts)

Create a script to apply `087_fix_code_arena_rls_recursion.sql` automatically to the postgres instance using `DATABASE_URL` / `DIRECT_URL`.

